      "description": "Watch Chelsea vs Hull City highlights and goals from Premier League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 12, 2026. The Premier League clash on 2026-09-12 brought a high-octane atmosphere to the capital, as two sides hungry for momentum faced off in a compelling encounter. From the first whistle, the game unfolded as a tactical chess match punctuated by moments of individual brilliance and defensive frailty. Rapid Exchanges and a Quickfire Double Chelsea wasted no time in asserting their presence, breaking the deadlock in the 7th minute. Following a defensive lapse by Emiliano Martinez , the home side clinical. Cole Palmer provided the vision with a key pass, allowing Joao Pedro to set up Morgan Rogers , who slotted home with his left foot. However, the lead proved fragile as Hull City mounted a spirited comeback before the interval. Mohamed Belloumi turned the game on its head in a sensational six-minute spell. In the 28th minute, he capitalized on a mistake by Jorrel Hato to level the scores after being found by Ryan Giles . Belloumi wasn't finished, and in the 34th minute, he struck again with his left foot, this time assisted by Oli McBurnie , sending the traveling supporters into raptures as the Tigers took an unexpected lead into the break. Second Half Resilience and Late Drama The second half saw Chelsea dominate possession, reaching a 68% share as they hunted for an equalizer. Their persistence paid off in the 66th minute; Cole Palmer turned provider once more, finding Joao Pedro , who maintained his composure to fire home the leveling goal. The match grew increasingly physical thereafter, with the referee busy issuing bookings to players including John Egan , Matt Crooks , and Valentin Barco as both teams fought for every inch of grass. As the clock ticked into six minutes of added time, the drama intensified for the 39,352 fans in attendance. Estevao forced a fine save from the keeper in the 91st minute, and Cole Palmer had a golden opportunity to win it with a late free kick, but his effort sailed wide. Despite a late flurry of corners and a yellow card for Brooke Norton-Cuffy in the dying moments, neither side could find a winner, leaving the points shared in a hard-fought contest."
